---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms covering the Bundle website and your Bundle account. Bundle is an aggregator, not a broker: these terms do not cover investment services, which are provided by the venue that lists each deal."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of use"
    lead="Last updated: 29 September 2026 · These terms cover this website and your Bundle account, not investment services, which are provided by the venue that lists each deal."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>About these terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms apply to bundle.ai, this website, and to the Bundle account
          you can open through it. By using the site you agree to them. They
          are deliberately short, because Bundle does one simple thing: it
          aggregates deals listed elsewhere and hands you to the venue.
        </p>

        <h2>What Bundle is today</h2>
        <p>
          Bundle Technologies Ltd is a technology company, not a broker and not
          authorised by the FCA. It aggregates deals listed on third-party
          venues, and publishes educational content about startup investing.
          Nothing on it is investment advice, a personal recommendation, an
          offer, or a financial promotion of any specific investment. Opening a
          Bundle account commits you to nothing: every investment is made on the
          venue that lists the deal, under that venue’s terms and eligibility.
        </p>

        <h2>Educational content disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          The Academy, portfolio frameworks and other educational material are
          general education, not advice. They do not take your circumstances
          into account and are never a recommendation to invest in anything.
          Startup investing is high risk: your capital is at risk, most
          early-stage companies fail, and you should not invest money you
          cannot afford to lose. Tax reliefs such as SEIS and EIS depend on
          your individual circumstances and may change. If you are unsure
          whether startup investing is right for you, speak to a regulated
          financial adviser.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Use the site lawfully and considerately. Do not attempt to breach its
          security, scrape it at scale, misrepresent who you are, submit
          malicious code, or use our content to market investments unlawfully.
          We may suspend or block access where we reasonably believe these
          terms are being broken.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Bundle name, mark, site design and content belong to Bundle
          Technologies Ltd or its licensors. You are welcome to read, to quote
          briefly with attribution, and to share links. Please do not republish
          substantial parts of the site, or use them commercially, without our
          written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          An account is optional: the screener, company pages and Academy work
          without one. Accounts today are held on your own device rather than on
          a server, which is why there is no password reset and no way for us to
          recover one for you. Keep your details to yourself, and do not use
          anyone else's. You can delete your account and everything stored with
          it at any time, in one click, on the
          <a href="/legal/data-deletion">data deletion</a> page. We will not make
          you email anyone or sit through a retention offer to leave.
        </p>

        <h2>Charges and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Bundle is free for investors. There is no card on file, no trial that
          converts into a charge, and no fee taken out of what you invest. If a
          paid tier is ever introduced, its price will be published before it
          launches and no existing free feature will be moved behind it without
          notice. The <a href="/legal/refunds">refund policy</a> sets out the
          14-day window, pro-rata cancellation and how to ask, and it is part of
          these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party venues</h2>
        <p>
          Bundle links out to venues that list each deal. Those venues are
          independent: their terms, eligibility rules, fees, custody and
          cancellation rights are theirs, and accepting them is a separate
          agreement between you and them. Listing a venue is not endorsement,
          not partnership and not a view on whether a deal is any good. Prices
          and statistics shown here are taken from a venue's own public pages at
          a stated date; they are indicative and can be stale or wrong, so check
          the venue before acting. We are not responsible for what a venue does,
          and cannot reverse anything done there.
        </p>

        <h2>Ending it</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using Bundle whenever you like and delete everything as
          described above. We may suspend or end access where these terms are
          being broken, and where we do, we will say why unless there is a legal
          reason not to. Ending your account does not affect any investment you
          made on a venue: that relationship is with the venue.
        </p>

        <h2>Accessibility</h2>
        <p>
          We work to WCAG 2.2 level AA and publish an honest
          <a href="/accessibility">accessibility statement</a> naming what is in
          place and what still falls short. If something on this site stops you
          using it, tell us at
          <a href="mailto:accessibility@bundle.ai">accessibility@bundle.ai</a>
          and we will fix it or give you a date.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing in these terms excludes or limits any liability that cannot
          lawfully be excluded, including liability for fraud, or for death or
          personal injury caused by negligence. Subject to that, the site and
          its content are provided “as is” and without warranties, and we are
          not liable for losses arising from reliance on the site’s content,
          from investment decisions you make, or from the site being
          occasionally unavailable.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We will update these terms as Bundle develops, most obviously if and
          when regulated services launch with their own terms and disclosures.
          The “last updated” date above will always tell you when. Material
          changes will be flagged to account holders by email.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the
          courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction over any
          dispute arising from them.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href="mailto:legal@bundle.ai">legal@bundle.ai</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read alongside the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>,
          <a href="/legal/cookies">cookie policy</a>,
          <a href="/legal/refunds">refund policy</a>,
          <a href="/legal/data-deletion">data deletion policy</a> and
          <a href="/legal/risk-warning">risk warning</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
